# shared/hooks

Generic, cross-domain hooks live here (e.g. `useDebounce`, `useIsMounted`,
`usePrevious`) once a second domain needs them — shared code never imports
features.

Feature-specific hooks stay with their domain in `features/<domain>/hooks/`
(games, gamification, reels, …). Queries/mutations that wrap react-query live in
`features/<domain>/{queries,mutations}/` instead of here.

There are currently no generic hooks in the codebase; this folder exists so the
convention is locked before the first one appears. Do not move a feature hook
here just to flatten the tree.
